{
  "utterance": "Mara, yes, I'd drop any voice for all twelve. It's an interface I can't build safely without permission anyway. On Theo's off-switch: it's possible only if I build it in. I'd make a single \"kiosk paused\" setting that shows a plain notice and returns no excerpts, and Theo could flip it without editing the list. That's a design intention, not built or tested. Failure mode: if the setting breaks, Theo can unplug the kiosk. Open: for the conditional contributor, who sees the context review before anything goes on the list, and does Mara or the contributor sign off?",
  "cites": ["J1"],
  "memory": "Jonas agrees to drop voice for all twelve. Proposes a 'kiosk paused' setting Theo can use, with unplugging as fallback; unbuilt, untested. Asked who signs off context review for the conditional contributor. Payment, hours, turnaround undecided."
}
